      "id": 140549,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-21T14:05:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I understand they don't want to handcuff new big profit material, but a large part of the selling point of the expanded universe stuff was it being canonical.</p><p>I guess it is pretty easy to go back on that now that big money is on the line, but it is a crappy move for fans that know so much canon that is no longer canon. &nbsp;Now you can go spend money to see the new canon. &nbsp;At least until they redact it.</p><p>It's like \"come get your new Star Wars canon before we redact it in the name of profit!\"</p><p>Yeah, I'm bitter.</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:17:28.963Z",
